# Who reviews what, and why.
#
# A visual baseline is a decision, not an artifact: whoever can change it decides what counts
# as a regression. So the two things that together define the gate — the approved bundle and
# the workflow that enforces it — are reviewed by the project owner by default.
#
# GitHub only applies this if the base branch requires review from code owners; see
# docs/BASELINE-UPDATES.md for the settings that have to be enabled by hand.

# The canonical approved baselines. A change here changes what every future pull request is
# compared against.
/examples/uiproof-baselines/ @Azmk1

# The gate itself: the workflow, the pinned rendering environment and scripts the gate runs.
/.github/workflows/visual-regression.yml @Azmk1
/.github/workflows/baseline-update.yml @Azmk1
/scripts/ci/ @Azmk1
